<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase") at VFEP commit e237aba (2026-08-29),
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml. Everything not listed under
    "Tuning" below is still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy (placeholder, per
    TODOs.md). See Warcasket_Shipcracker.xml's header for the Odyssey patch
    findings and the WarcasketVeteran/WarcasketAll tag research; the same
    conclusion applies here.

    Tuning (2026-09-13): costList Plasteel 70 (Siegebreaker 60). Follows the
    armor's Plasteel rise to 165 at the shoulder-to-armor ratio the 10th-gen
    sets use, roughly 0.4 (Siegebreaker 60/145, Guardian 80/200, Controller
    60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145, Brute 60/160): 0.4 x 165 = 66, rounded up to
    the 10-plasteel steps VFEP's costLists use. No spacer components, like the
    Siegebreaker, Guardian and Sarcophagus shoulders.

    Abilities (2026-09-16, design approved that day): the breaching arms.
    - SCWC_BreachPower +0.5: the armor's Breach Jump landing deals 45 to pawns and
      900 to structures with these on (30 / 600 without), enough for plasteel and
      uranium walls; see 1.6/Defs/StatDefs/BreachPower.xml.
    - equippedStatFactors MeleeHitChance x1.15 and MeleeDodgeChance x1.15 through
      VEF's ApparelExtension (Shock's shoulders use x1.2 on the same pair), merged
      with the base's extension the way VFEP's own sets do it.
    - No jump-range contribution: a space-centric piece, and the range lives on
      the armor. The Siegebreaker's EnergyShieldRechargeRate +1 was dropped: VEF's
      CompShieldBubble reads that stat off the apparel, never the pawn, so the
      offset never reached the shield (dead XML in VFEP too).
    - costList GravlitePanel 10 under Odyssey; see the armor's header for the split.

    SOS2/Universum: our 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml deliberately leaves shoulder
    pads alone, mirroring VFEP's own patch, which only touches armor and helmets.
    Vanilla Gravship Expanded: our VGE1 vacuum patch (see the armor's header)
    leaves the shoulders' 0.1 alone, exactly as VGE1 leaves VFEP's.
    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders
    (+ _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring
    VFEP's own warcasket layout.

    Draw order (2026-09-16): dataNorth offset y 0.05 (base 0.2). A worn apparel
    node's altitude is its drawData offset's y (added verbatim by
    PawnRenderTree.TryGetMatrix) plus PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer(layer),
    0.000366 per layer unit, where the layer is the ApparelBody node's 20 plus the
    piece's index among body apparel; the y offsets VFEP's bases carry are what
    actually order the pieces. With the base's 0.2 the pauldrons sit over the shell
    in the north view (0.2 vs 0.1). This art wants the shell's back frame over the
    pauldron inner edges, so this piece drops below the shell there: about 0.058
    against the shell's 0.107, still well above the bodysuit (VEF's
    secondaryApparelGraphics feeds VFEP_Warcasket_Bodysuit through vanilla
    ProcessApparel with that def's own null drawData, so it stays near 0.008 in
    every facing and is untouched by either set's offsets), the helmet (0.026 in
    the north, where the head chain has no y offset) and pack-layer apparel (layer
    93, 0.034). Lowering the pauldrons rather than raising the armor keeps the
    armor at VFEP's standard altitude for foundry mix-and-match with VFEP sets.
    South/east/west inherit the base's 0.02. Only the facing that changes is
    listed: XmlInheritance merges same-named elements recursively, so the other
    three RotationalData entries come through from VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>SCWC_WarcasketShoulders_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Placeholder shipcracker warcasket pauldrons. Stats are an untuned copy of the siegebreaker warcasket shoulders for now.</shortDescription>
    <description>Placeholder description for the shipcracker warcasket pauldrons. It is a stand-in for later tuning, not lore.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachPower>0.5</SCWC_BreachPower>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <Plasteel>70</Plasteel>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">10</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <!-- Under the shell in the north view; see "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataNorth><offset>(0, 0.05, 0)</offset></dataNorth>
      </drawData>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <equippedStatFactors>
          <MeleeHitChance>1.15</MeleeHitChance>
          <MeleeDodgeChance>1.15</MeleeDodgeChance>
        </equippedStatFactors>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
